500
00:33:47,849 --> 00:33:49,183
- Sorry, sorry.
- It's okay.

501
00:33:51,853 --> 00:33:52,687
Hi, hi.

502
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:53,721
Your classroom is over there.

503
00:33:54,556 --> 00:33:55,623
- Oh, good morning.
- Good morning.

504
00:33:55,723 --> 00:33:56,457
Good morning.

505
00:33:56,558 --> 00:33:58,860
<i>What is his flashback sob story
to get sloshed every day?</i>

506
00:33:58,893 --> 00:33:59,894
Don't you ever ask him this.

507
00:34:00,195 --> 00:34:01,529
If he gets a gullible idiot,

508
00:34:01,563 --> 00:34:03,231
he'll reel off
a Mani Ratnam classic as his own!

509
00:34:03,264 --> 00:34:05,833
Fell head over heels, followed her
wherever she went.

510
00:34:05,934 --> 00:34:09,604
She also reciprocated and one day while
we were happily sitting in a coffee shop,

511
00:34:10,238 --> 00:34:11,172
her father walked in!

512
00:34:11,272 --> 00:34:13,608
- Did you get caught?
- Patience, Sister.

513
00:34:13,641 --> 00:34:14,809
Her father's name

514
00:34:14,976 --> 00:34:16,144
is Mr Chandramouli.

515
00:34:16,311 --> 00:34:17,979
We were both neighbors
in Rainbow Colony.

516
00:34:18,112 --> 00:34:19,981
I was in 8G.
She was in 7G.

517
00:34:20,148 --> 00:34:21,316
India is here.

518
00:34:21,983 --> 00:34:23,685
America is over there.

519
00:34:23,851 --> 00:34:27,522
That's why I started playing guitar.
She was the love of my life.

520
00:34:27,555 --> 00:34:29,624
We climbed up straight to
the top of the mountain.

521
00:34:29,724 --> 00:34:31,893
We decided to jump
on the count of five.

522
00:34:32,227 --> 00:34:34,562
My bad luck I got stuck
in a tree and escaped death.

523
00:34:34,696 --> 00:34:35,563
What?

524
00:34:36,397 --> 00:34:38,399
Her head hit a boulder and she died.

525
00:34:38,566 --> 00:34:40,268
- That's a Kamal classic. Don't bug me
- Hey!

526
00:34:40,435 --> 00:34:41,603
This is all too much.

527
00:34:42,737 --> 00:34:44,272
Okay, which department is he in?

528
00:34:44,606 --> 00:34:47,141
He studied in this very college.
He graduated in M.Phil Psychology.

529
00:34:47,308 --> 00:34:49,644
<i>Now he teaches Personality Development.</i>

530
00:34:49,777 --> 00:34:51,813
May I request you all to please stand up?

531
00:34:53,181 --> 00:34:55,316
I said stand up.

532
00:34:55,683 --> 00:34:59,187
Now I intend on checking
if your mind and body are focused.

533
00:34:59,320 --> 00:35:00,355
We are hearing.

534
00:35:01,689 --> 00:35:02,790
But not listening.

535
00:35:02,891 --> 00:35:06,227
Students don't listen to their teachers.
Teachers don't listen to their students.

536
00:35:06,694 --> 00:35:08,062
Now, run!

537
00:35:08,897 --> 00:35:10,565
Run, run, run, run!

538
00:35:10,732 --> 00:35:11,599
Water!

539
00:35:13,268 --> 00:35:14,269
Electricity!

540
00:35:16,404 --> 00:35:19,807
Children don't listen to their parents.
Parents don't listen to their children.

541
00:35:20,141 --> 00:35:21,209
And finally,

542
00:35:21,309 --> 00:35:23,311
...doesn't listen to their people.

543
00:35:23,611 --> 00:35:26,180
Repeat whatever I tell you now verbatim

544
00:35:26,648 --> 00:35:29,183
but do it the opposite way.

545
00:35:29,350 --> 00:35:30,852
- Jump in!
- Jump in!

546
00:35:30,985 --> 00:35:32,520
- Jump left!
- Jump left!

547
00:35:32,687 --> 00:35:34,189
Jump right. Hey!

548
00:35:34,689 --> 00:35:35,890
Now on the starboard.

549
00:35:36,724 --> 00:35:37,892
Faster, faster, faster!

550
00:35:38,059 --> 00:35:40,195
Now close your bloody eyes and freeze!

551
00:35:46,434 --> 00:35:47,268
Class disperse.

552
00:35:47,435 --> 00:35:48,603
Thank God.

553
00:35:49,604 --> 00:35:50,605
I'm getting late for my class.

554
00:35:50,772 --> 00:35:52,473
- We'll meet at lunch.
- Okay, sure.

555
00:35:57,812 --> 00:35:59,080
Let me repeat this.

556
00:35:59,147 --> 00:36:01,516
That bloody Bhavani is
responsible for all this.

557
00:36:01,683 --> 00:36:04,852
He finished off his opponents contesting
in our Union Election one by one.

558
00:36:05,019 --> 00:36:06,855
I know his history A to Z.

559
00:36:06,988 --> 00:36:10,225
Gurumurthy, whether these people
understand it or not, hope you do.

560
00:36:11,025 --> 00:36:12,894
I have been saying this
right from the beginning.

561
00:36:13,061 --> 00:36:13,962
Who endorsed my view?

562
00:36:14,062 --> 00:36:16,598
With the help of the juvenile delinquents,
he's engaging in criminal activities.

563
00:36:16,731 --> 00:36:17,899
Has the cat got your tongue or what?

564
00:36:17,932 --> 00:36:20,268
- Tell them.
- We've been saying the same--

565
00:36:32,347 --> 00:36:33,314
Hello, sir.

566
00:36:34,515 --> 00:36:35,683
Damn you!

567
00:36:36,184 --> 00:36:38,019
Are you such a big shot, huh?

568
00:36:38,987 --> 00:36:41,189
If you kill him, will you get his post?

569
00:36:41,689 --> 00:36:43,358
- Let me see.
- No, Brother.

570
00:36:43,391 --> 00:36:45,693
Why are you so mad at me?
I'm like a brother to you.

571
00:36:45,727 --> 00:36:46,961
Whatever it is, let's talk it over.

572
00:36:47,061 --> 00:36:48,830
Any need for me to talk to you?

573
00:36:48,897 --> 00:36:49,964
I'm going to kill you.

574
00:36:50,064 --> 00:36:51,099
Get the car ready.

575
00:36:51,232 --> 00:36:53,101
Brother, will a problem
be solved if we fight?

576
00:36:53,268 --> 00:36:55,503
Will murder solve the problem?
Let's discuss it amicably.

577
00:36:55,603 --> 00:36:59,040
I'll use the same juvenile delinquents
you use as a tool to finish you off!

578
00:36:59,140 --> 00:37:00,108
Wait and watch?

579
00:37:00,141 --> 00:37:01,976
I grew up right before your eyes, sir.

580
00:37:02,110 --> 00:37:03,878
- Wait, sir.
- You peed in your pants scared of me.

581
00:37:03,978 --> 00:37:05,480
You think you're my equal now?

582
00:37:05,513 --> 00:37:07,181
Whatever it is, let's talk it over.

583
00:37:07,315 --> 00:37:09,584
I am much younger than you,
but pay heed to my words.

584
00:37:09,684 --> 00:37:10,852
Don't go--

585
00:37:11,519 --> 00:37:12,587
Oh, my God!

586
00:37:12,687 --> 00:37:14,022
Gone.

587
00:37:14,856 --> 00:37:16,024
Catch that lorry driver.

588
00:37:21,896 --> 00:37:22,964
So sad.

589
00:37:23,064 --> 00:37:24,132
You were eye witnesses.

590
00:37:24,232 --> 00:37:25,233
What did I do?

591
00:37:25,934 --> 00:37:28,169
If I had walked out talking to him,
I would've shared his fate.

592
00:37:28,269 --> 00:37:30,104
Impossible for a human
to time this so perfectly.

593
00:37:30,271 --> 00:37:31,940
I pray to all Gods thrice daily.

594
00:37:31,973 --> 00:37:33,975
So God has saved me
and punished him.

595
00:37:34,642 --> 00:37:36,110
He was a good soul!

596
00:37:38,479 --> 00:37:40,648
To conduct students' election
in our college this year,

597
00:37:41,182 --> 00:37:45,353
University Grants Commission has granted
permission, but I opposed it strictly.

598
00:37:46,154 --> 00:37:50,225
That's why for a mere formality
I need all your opinions on

599
00:37:50,859 --> 00:37:52,694
why we don't want the election.

600
00:37:52,727 --> 00:37:53,728
For the records.

601
00:37:54,729 --> 00:37:56,397
I somehow feel it is unnecessary, sir.

602
00:37:56,564 --> 00:37:57,765
Semester is fast approaching.

603
00:37:57,899 --> 00:37:59,901
In the current scenario,
why do we need an election?

604
00:37:59,934 --> 00:38:02,270
Sir, if this happens, it will
create some other issue.

605
00:38:02,437 --> 00:38:04,439
- I don't think they are fit for elections.
- Exactly.

606
00:38:04,806 --> 00:38:06,608
In my honest opinion, no.

607
00:38:06,641 --> 00:38:09,110
<i>I have no issues with
the day college students.</i>

608
00:38:09,143 --> 00:38:11,312
<i>I am a little apprehensive
about the evening batch.</i>

609
00:38:11,446 --> 00:38:12,480
Thanks, Ramya.

610
00:38:12,647 --> 00:38:13,648
Charulatha, your opinion?

611
00:38:13,815 --> 00:38:16,684
Sir, I joined the college
two weeks ago.

612
00:38:17,018 --> 00:38:19,587
I don't know if it'd be right for me
to voice my opinion at the moment.

613
00:38:19,687 --> 00:38:21,222
Come on, what's there?

614
00:38:22,357 --> 00:38:23,625
- No, sir.
- Hey!

615
00:38:23,725 --> 00:38:25,727
- Why is JD sir keeping quiet?
- That's right?

616
00:38:26,060 --> 00:38:28,897
- He's waiting to make a good point.
- I don't think election is a good idea.

617
00:38:28,930 --> 00:38:31,933
Sir, to be on the safe side,
ask JD his opinion.

618
00:38:35,403 --> 00:38:37,472
JD, tell us your opinion.

619
00:38:42,644 --> 00:38:44,712
What is your opinion, JD?

620
00:38:44,812 --> 00:38:46,981
- What day was yesterday?
- Thursday.

621
00:38:47,015 --> 00:38:48,583
Thursday is his day off.

622
00:38:48,683 --> 00:38:50,652
- Professor JD.
- He would have been piss drunk.

623
00:38:50,685 --> 00:38:52,854
- Come, come
- Hey, careful!

624
00:38:53,855 --> 00:38:55,056
JD?

625
00:38:56,891 --> 00:38:57,725
Sir!

626
00:38:58,226 --> 00:38:59,360
Emergency, sir.

627
00:38:59,394 --> 00:39:00,461
What are you doing here?

628
00:39:00,562 --> 00:39:02,430
Let me give this phone to Rosie ma'am.

629
00:39:02,564 --> 00:39:04,265
Her husband fell off his bike.

630
00:39:04,399 --> 00:39:05,567
What the hell are you doing?

631
00:39:05,600 --> 00:39:06,668
I will expel you.

632
00:39:06,768 --> 00:39:09,270
- Let her just talk to him.
- What happened, Abdul?

633
00:39:09,437 --> 00:39:10,171
Wake up, sir.

634
00:39:10,271 --> 00:39:11,873
- Tell me!
- Don't switch off your phone.

635
00:39:11,940 --> 00:39:12,974
Talk to him.

636
00:39:13,141 --> 00:39:14,609
- Poor husband.
- One minute, sir.

637
00:39:14,642 --> 00:39:16,644
They are objecting to elections.
Support us, sir.

638
00:39:17,612 --> 00:39:18,613
- Sorry, sir.
- Get out!

639
00:39:18,646 --> 00:39:20,014
- Useless fellow!
- Thank you, sir.

640
00:39:21,683 --> 00:39:23,985
JD, what is your opinion
about conducting elections?

641
00:39:24,018 --> 00:39:26,521
Election is essential. That's all.

642
00:39:27,355 --> 00:39:29,891
- I knew it.
- He will say something meaningless, sir.

643
00:39:30,024 --> 00:39:33,728
If we announce a students' election,
all of them will be thinking of only that.

644
00:39:33,895 --> 00:39:36,598
None of them will study
nor will anyone attend any class.

645
00:39:36,731 --> 00:39:39,934
Correct. What will they learn
by conducting students' election?

646
00:39:40,735 --> 00:39:42,270
Why encourage politics in college?

647
00:39:43,071 --> 00:39:43,805
Matthew sir.

648
00:39:44,639 --> 00:39:45,773
What is politics, sir?

649
00:39:46,641 --> 00:39:48,309
Sir, I don't wish to talk to you.

650
00:39:48,810 --> 00:39:50,144
Is that so? But I wish to speak.

651
00:39:50,445 --> 00:39:51,479
I'm coming.

652
00:39:54,482 --> 00:39:55,516
Sir.

653
00:39:56,351 --> 00:39:58,987
First, a student should know
politics means service.

654
00:39:59,020 --> 00:40:02,690
Only if our students learn about election,
canvassing, leadership in college.

655
00:40:02,724 --> 00:40:05,793
they will have an awareness about
state, central elections in the future.

656
00:40:05,894 --> 00:40:08,396
College students are first time voters.

657
00:40:09,063 --> 00:40:10,398
Only if they are allowed to think,

658
00:40:10,565 --> 00:40:12,600
a new leader will emerge
for the next generation.

659
00:40:12,767 --> 00:40:15,336
To be molded as a good leader
or to choose the right leader,

660
00:40:15,436 --> 00:40:17,438
they will acquire
both tact and discretion.

661
00:40:17,639 --> 00:40:18,773
- For someone to--
- Sir.

662
00:40:19,307 --> 00:40:21,809
They will stick posters all over
and spoil the walls with graffiti.

663
00:40:21,943 --> 00:40:23,778
Then claim ownership
over the walls and fight.

664
00:40:23,811 --> 00:40:25,847
Doesn't all this happen
in normal elections?

665
00:40:25,980 --> 00:40:26,981
Sit down, sir.

666
00:40:28,016 --> 00:40:30,752
Aren't these things common in elections?

667
00:40:30,852 --> 00:40:33,187
Can we abolish elections
in our country for this reason?

668
00:40:33,354 --> 00:40:36,224
We have grown up with this culture of
poster, banner and still follow it.

669
00:40:36,891 --> 00:40:40,128
For students to know
the do's and don'ts with posters,

670
00:40:40,228 --> 00:40:42,063
we must conduct
elections in college.

671
00:40:42,397 --> 00:40:43,998
Only then they will
do well in the outside world.

672
00:40:44,098 --> 00:40:48,102
If our culture of bribing with biriyani
booze and big bucks should change,

673
00:40:48,436 --> 00:40:50,672
students should know
the in and out of politics.

674
00:40:50,772 --> 00:40:51,773
Okay.

675
00:40:52,106 --> 00:40:53,775
Let's assume what you're saying is right.

676
00:40:53,808 --> 00:40:58,646
Who is responsible if students resort
to violence or damage college property?

677
00:40:58,813 --> 00:41:00,848
Sir, nothing of that sort will happen.

678
00:41:01,015 --> 00:41:03,484
If you are proved wrong,
will you leave this college?

679
00:41:03,818 --> 00:41:05,820
Will you resign, huh?

680
00:41:06,354 --> 00:41:07,722
I'll think about it if it happens.

681
00:41:07,889 --> 00:41:09,858
Then you be the presiding officer

682
00:41:10,225 --> 00:41:11,226
and conduct the election.

683
00:41:12,060 --> 00:41:13,561
If any problem crops up,

684
00:41:14,062 --> 00:41:16,397
you have to leave the college.
Give this in writing.

685
00:41:22,604 --> 00:41:25,273
Coming June 25th
Students' elections.

686
00:41:29,310 --> 00:41:32,013
I haven't seen him conduct
an election as a master.

687
00:41:32,146 --> 00:41:34,816
But I've seen him
do the same as a student.

688
00:41:44,225 --> 00:41:45,059
Shake your hands.

689
00:41:51,266 --> 00:41:52,934
This is the wall of democracy.

690
00:41:53,101 --> 00:41:54,569
Your rules and regulations.

691
00:41:59,140 --> 00:42:00,975
Gym facilities free for all students.

692
00:42:01,109 --> 00:42:03,278
Meat will be served for all in the hostel.

693
00:42:03,645 --> 00:42:05,813
Good orators have become able leaders.

694
00:42:05,847 --> 00:42:07,515
You should speak up more boldly, Savi.

695
00:42:07,649 --> 00:42:09,918
<i>Instead of finding faults
with your rival,</i>

696
00:42:10,018 --> 00:42:12,153
<i>ask for votes
listing your reforms.</i>

697
00:42:12,854 --> 00:42:15,290
Tear every single poster, dude.

698
00:42:15,356 --> 00:42:18,059
Posters and banners should be stuck
or erected in their allocated places.

699
00:42:18,359 --> 00:42:20,461
Even if there's a small brawl
among the students,

700
00:42:20,562 --> 00:42:21,563
election will be canceled.

701
00:42:23,398 --> 00:42:25,934
You pull back and fire.

702
00:42:26,067 --> 00:42:26,901
Cheers!

703
00:42:27,101 --> 00:42:29,070
Our total strength is 5500 students, sir.

704
00:42:29,270 --> 00:42:31,105
We have divided them into 10 categories.

705
00:42:31,940 --> 00:42:32,974
What is this column?

706
00:42:33,141 --> 00:42:35,610
That is the religion and caste category.

707
00:42:35,977 --> 00:42:36,945
Let's avoid that.

708
00:42:37,312 --> 00:42:39,647
We have to remove this from here

709
00:42:40,014 --> 00:42:41,849
to ensure it doesn't follow us
wherever we go.

710
00:42:44,485 --> 00:42:47,522
How much longer do you intend on
drinking and loitering around?

711
00:42:47,689 --> 00:42:49,023
Why yell at me for no reason?

712
00:42:49,390 --> 00:42:50,892
Will I yell at you
if you are steady on your feet?

713
00:42:53,728 --> 00:42:55,730
- I am sober.
- Is that so?

714
00:42:57,232 --> 00:42:59,000
Hit an arrow
anywhere on this board.

715
00:42:59,100 --> 00:43:00,568
I'll agree you are sober and steady.

716
00:43:01,102 --> 00:43:03,071
Dude, aim for the bull's eye.

717
00:43:13,481 --> 00:43:15,316
One lakh rupees to students
in each department.

718
00:43:15,350 --> 00:43:16,317
Cheers!

719
00:43:16,351 --> 00:43:17,852
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

720
00:43:17,986 --> 00:43:20,255
I have a fair amount of
experience in counselling.

721
00:43:20,355 --> 00:43:24,125
If you can tell me the reason,
I can do my level best to help you.

722
00:43:24,225 --> 00:43:27,061
You know, when I was jobless,

723
00:43:28,363 --> 00:43:30,632
I hanged around
a tiles company in Rajasthan.

724
00:43:30,732 --> 00:43:32,166
- Oh!
- At that time,

725
00:43:32,267 --> 00:43:34,769
a girl lost her bag in the train.

726
00:43:35,436 --> 00:43:37,605
I found it and sent it to her.

727
00:43:38,273 --> 00:43:39,974
She liked me for the effort I took.

728
00:43:41,309 --> 00:43:44,779
She and I became pen pals
and we fell in love

729
00:43:45,847 --> 00:43:48,516
then when she knew
I was in Rajasthan.

730
00:43:48,650 --> 00:43:50,318
For my sake, that girl knitted

731
00:43:50,351 --> 00:43:53,855
an embroidered sweater for me
and sent it to me.

732
00:43:54,355 --> 00:43:55,857
Sweater in Rajasthan!

733
00:43:58,059 --> 00:43:59,060
True.

734
00:44:08,603 --> 00:44:10,505
Tomorrow if you have a problem
and you come to me,

735
00:44:10,605 --> 00:44:12,473
even if it's midnight,
I'll be there for you.

736
00:44:12,607 --> 00:44:15,610
Why should we create problems
and end up in the police station?

737
00:44:15,643 --> 00:44:17,111
Beverages free in the canteen.

738
00:44:17,979 --> 00:44:19,314
Aqua training access free.

739
00:44:19,347 --> 00:44:20,648
You will have campus interviews.

740
00:44:20,815 --> 00:44:22,650
You'll leave the college
with a job in hand.

741
00:44:22,684 --> 00:44:24,185
Above all give this a serious thought.

742
00:44:24,686 --> 00:44:26,354
Do you want to be ruled by a girl?

743
00:44:27,021 --> 00:44:28,056
Or revel in a boy's leadership?

744
00:44:32,227 --> 00:44:35,230
Hey, that isn't even my glass.

745
00:44:35,396 --> 00:44:37,899
Some other chap had relished
his drink and is gone you madcap!

746
00:44:37,932 --> 00:44:39,067
How dare you!

747
00:44:39,601 --> 00:44:40,768
One JD, please.

748
00:44:59,854 --> 00:45:02,190
The third round of votes
have been counted.

749
00:45:02,557 --> 00:45:04,692
We have started counting
for the fourth round.

750
00:45:08,229 --> 00:45:09,097
Sir?

751
00:45:09,264 --> 00:45:10,498
Fourth round, sir.

752
00:45:10,598 --> 00:45:12,267
Results are due any moment.

753
00:45:13,101 --> 00:45:14,102
I'm scared, sir.

754
00:45:19,107 --> 00:45:20,975
Are you Satyaraj acting
as Amavasai in Amaidhi Padai?

755
00:45:21,442 --> 00:45:22,310
"Fourth round!"

756
00:45:22,644 --> 00:45:23,478
Get lost.

757
00:45:23,778 --> 00:45:27,148
<i>Most awaiting election results
are going to be declared very soon.</i>

758
00:45:31,686 --> 00:45:34,389
<i>Fourth and final election results
are going to be declared.</i>

759
00:45:35,557 --> 00:45:38,226
Bhargav 2588 votes.

760
00:45:38,560 --> 00:45:40,695
<i>Savitha 2648 votes.</i>

761
00:45:40,895 --> 00:45:43,231
<i>Savitha won the election by 60 votes.</i>

762
00:46:00,315 --> 00:46:01,849
Congratulations, Chairperson.

763
00:46:02,517 --> 00:46:05,520
Sir, I think they have already
started creating a ruckus there.

764
00:46:05,653 --> 00:46:06,988
Sir, what do we do now?

765
00:46:07,021 --> 00:46:09,557
Why do you still ask me?
She's the captain of your ship.

766
00:46:09,891 --> 00:46:11,559
Chairman, tell us what to do?

767
00:46:13,561 --> 00:46:14,562
Sir...

768
00:46:14,696 --> 00:46:16,564
To avoid all these unnecessary confusion,

769
00:46:16,598 --> 00:46:18,766
I'm thinking of talking
to Bhargav in person.

770
00:46:19,434 --> 00:46:20,568
Look at that!

771
00:46:20,735 --> 00:46:22,070
By all means go and talk.

772
00:46:22,237 --> 00:46:23,438
But go alone.

773
00:46:24,606 --> 00:46:25,273
Madam.

774
00:46:25,640 --> 00:46:28,877
Don't dilly-dally, scratch your head,
crack your knuckles and keep looking back.

775
00:46:28,977 --> 00:46:30,645
Don't dawdle and
do instalment walk.

776
00:46:30,778 --> 00:46:31,813
Forward march!

777
00:46:34,682 --> 00:46:37,685
Sir, will you give me your bracelet?

778
00:46:37,986 --> 00:46:38,920
Why?

779
00:46:39,020 --> 00:46:40,688
- Please give, sir.
- Dude, play that song.

780
00:46:42,023 --> 00:46:46,060
<i>Look! We must lead a life like that bird
Without a care in the world</i>

781
00:46:46,561 --> 00:46:50,765
<i>We should go on a dancing spree
Like the waves here in glee</i>

782
00:46:51,266 --> 00:46:55,603
<i>Under the same sky spacious
On the same land so precious</i>

783
00:46:55,737 --> 00:46:59,140
<i>Under the same sky endless
On our Motherland peerless</i>

784
00:47:03,811 --> 00:47:05,113
I want to talk to you.

785
00:47:05,313 --> 00:47:08,349
If she comes offering a truce,
I'll break the bones on her face.

786
00:47:12,520 --> 00:47:14,189
- Sir, tell me.
- What happened?

787
00:47:14,355 --> 00:47:15,557
Your son lost, sir.

788
00:47:15,890 --> 00:47:16,958
What?

789
00:47:17,058 --> 00:47:18,226
Bhargav...

790
00:47:19,060 --> 00:47:20,562
I came to congratulate.

791
00:47:21,229 --> 00:47:24,899
Winning by just 60 votes
is no big victory at all.

792
00:47:26,601 --> 00:47:28,436
Is there any rule in college
there should be only one chairman?

793
00:47:29,103 --> 00:47:31,940
You take over day college
and I'll handle evening college.

794
00:47:32,974 --> 00:47:33,975
Okay, bye.

795
00:47:35,643 --> 00:47:36,644
Congrats.

796
00:47:37,278 --> 00:47:39,214
I extended my hand
even on nomination day,

797
00:47:39,314 --> 00:47:40,982
but you weren't in the mood to shake.

798
00:47:43,851 --> 00:47:45,320
At least let there be truce now?

799
00:47:46,688 --> 00:47:48,523
I don't think it's safe
for her to go alone.

800
00:47:49,190 --> 00:47:50,391
Shall I go and check, sir?

801
00:47:59,601 --> 00:48:00,268
Let's shake hands.

802
00:48:01,936 --> 00:48:03,404
- Okay.
- How ridiculous.

803
00:48:03,605 --> 00:48:04,939
He has patched up happily.

804
00:48:05,273 --> 00:48:06,941
He is shaking hands
with that girl who won.

805
00:48:06,975 --> 00:48:07,976
<i>Let me talk to him.</i>

806
00:48:08,109 --> 00:48:09,110
One minute, sir.

807
00:48:09,143 --> 00:48:10,278
Bhargav.

808
00:48:11,312 --> 00:48:14,249
Dad, there's no problem.
I spoke to that girl.

809
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:16,017
She even asked me to be
the chairman for day college, Dad.

810
00:48:16,684 --> 00:48:19,354
<i>You got a sudden desire to
beg a post from her, huh?'</i>

811
00:48:19,687 --> 00:48:22,557
It isn't what you think, Dad.
I'll explain it to you in person.

812
00:48:25,360 --> 00:48:27,629
- Sir.
- <i>Pack him home in our car now.</i>

813
00:48:27,729 --> 00:48:28,563
Okay, sir.

814
00:48:28,696 --> 00:48:30,498
<i>If he refuses to go, threaten him.</i>

815
00:48:30,565 --> 00:48:33,268
<i>- Rough up that female who defeated him.</i>
- I'll handle it.

816
00:48:34,402 --> 00:48:36,771
I'll explain to my dad.
Please don't create a ruckus.

817
00:48:36,905 --> 00:48:39,474
He has given me permission
to scar even your face, sir.

818
00:48:39,607 --> 00:48:40,642
First, get inside.

819
00:48:41,142 --> 00:48:42,544
But please don't hurt that girl.

820
00:48:42,644 --> 00:48:44,445
Sir, he wasn't nasty to me.

821
00:48:44,479 --> 00:48:46,147
I shook hands and he said okay.

822
00:48:46,814 --> 00:48:47,916
That's all.

823
00:48:48,016 --> 00:48:49,017
Celebrations are done.

824
00:48:49,684 --> 00:48:51,185
- Hey! Catch.
- Sir.

825
00:48:51,686 --> 00:48:52,587
Wear those IDs.

826
00:48:52,687 --> 00:48:54,622
- Where's the booth?
- First floor, sir.

827
00:48:54,689 --> 00:48:55,890
Hurry up.

828
00:48:57,892 --> 00:48:59,627
Clear up all this mess
and then rock and roll.

829
00:48:59,727 --> 00:49:03,932
Sir, evening college students are
planning to burn down the booth.

830
00:49:13,641 --> 00:49:15,376
- Who is he?
- Professor, sir.

831
00:49:15,476 --> 00:49:17,145
- What?
- That wasn't a proper election.

832
00:49:17,278 --> 00:49:19,981
- We demand re-election or re-counting.
- Election is over. That's it.

833
00:49:20,014 --> 00:49:21,983
- Burn down the booth.
- Which department are you?

834
00:49:22,016 --> 00:49:23,751
- Come here.
- Stop this bloody idle talk.

835
00:49:23,851 --> 00:49:25,920
I'll kill you, son of a gun
I'll break all your teeth!

836
00:49:26,020 --> 00:49:27,455
- Sri, quiet!
- Give that bottle.

837
00:49:27,522 --> 00:49:28,690
- Wait.
- Sir!

838
00:49:30,692 --> 00:49:32,560
- Sir, let go of me!
- Shut up, all of you.

839
00:49:33,561 --> 00:49:34,696
I'm trying to make peace-

840
00:49:34,729 --> 00:49:36,431
Sir, move aside!

841
00:49:36,564 --> 00:49:38,933
Evening college chairman candidate
Bhargav wants to talk to you, sir.

842
00:49:39,400 --> 00:49:40,935
<i>My dad didn't listen to me.</i>

843
00:49:41,069 --> 00:49:43,605
He has sent about 60 party riff-raffs
to bash up everyone in the college.

844
00:49:43,638 --> 00:49:46,975
<i>They have merged with the students.
Ensure our college students are safe.</i>

845
00:49:52,013 --> 00:49:53,514
On the starboard!

846
00:49:53,982 --> 00:49:56,184
- Why are all of them spinning?
- What are they doing?

847
00:49:56,351 --> 00:49:58,419
Now close your bloody eyes and freeze!

848
00:49:58,519 --> 00:50:00,421
What is this? Tell us, sir.

849
00:50:00,522 --> 00:50:01,956
Sticking to the wall like glue?

850
00:50:02,023 --> 00:50:03,057
Move forward.

851
00:50:03,224 --> 00:50:04,225
They are doing the opposite.

852
00:50:04,726 --> 00:50:05,727
Wait, don't go.

853
00:50:10,765 --> 00:50:13,101
Send all the girls home safe.

854
00:50:13,268 --> 00:50:14,769
- Sir?
- Just do as I say.

855
00:50:15,737 --> 00:50:17,372
Hey! Take all of them
through the back door.

856
00:50:17,438 --> 00:50:18,973
Go, go, fast!

857
00:50:19,307 --> 00:50:20,308
Go now!

858
00:50:43,398 --> 00:50:44,599
Savitha, you go!

859
00:50:45,900 --> 00:50:47,268
Hey! That's the girl.

860
00:50:47,602 --> 00:50:48,269
Grab her!

861
00:50:54,309 --> 00:50:55,143
Savitha.

862
00:50:57,979 --> 00:50:59,147
Hey!

863
00:51:04,686 --> 00:51:06,020
Hey!

864
00:51:09,190 --> 00:51:10,725
Are you okay?

865
00:51:15,930 --> 00:51:17,098
Go in. Quick.

866
00:51:21,236 --> 00:51:23,605
Sir, students are all out of control.

867
00:51:29,477 --> 00:51:30,378
Let me go.

868
00:51:30,478 --> 00:51:32,146
- Take your hands off.
- Let go of me. Sir.

869
00:51:32,347 --> 00:51:33,514
Take your hands off!

870
00:51:37,352 --> 00:51:39,854
How dare you manhandle girls!

871
00:52:00,475 --> 00:52:01,609
Master!

872
00:52:23,731 --> 00:52:25,767
Nothing major, just a nail scratch.

873
00:52:26,100 --> 00:52:28,603
Meeting is being held in the library.

874
00:52:29,103 --> 00:52:30,271
Is everyone safe?

875
00:52:30,438 --> 00:52:31,606
I have checked with all the groups.

876
00:52:31,639 --> 00:52:32,607
They have texted me.

877
00:52:32,640 --> 00:52:35,877
The entire riot has been recorded
in our college CCTV cameras.

878
00:52:35,977 --> 00:52:37,545
Is he behaving like a professor?

879
00:52:37,645 --> 00:52:40,014
Excuse me, ma'am, you are only
talking about damage of property.

880
00:52:40,148 --> 00:52:42,750
Rowdies got together and
bashed up about five of our girls.

881
00:52:42,850 --> 00:52:44,752
What could all the teachers do?

882
00:52:44,852 --> 00:52:46,921
- No one came to stop them.
- Stop it, Charu.

883
00:52:47,021 --> 00:52:49,457
You haven't even completed
a month in the college.

884
00:52:49,557 --> 00:52:50,558
Just keep quiet.

885
00:52:51,392 --> 00:52:53,895
What the hell are they discussing?

886
00:52:54,395 --> 00:52:55,363
I'll be back.

887
00:52:55,763 --> 00:52:56,965
I'll talk to JD.

888
00:52:57,065 --> 00:52:58,900
Then we will take a call.

889
00:52:58,933 --> 00:53:02,003
If he comes back,
we will resign, sir.

890
00:53:02,103 --> 00:53:04,439
- No, Mr. Samuel-
- What's going on here?

891
00:53:04,472 --> 00:53:07,976
Sir, I have already given
a commitment that I'll resign.

892
00:53:08,109 --> 00:53:09,377
I'm just leaving this college.

893
00:53:09,477 --> 00:53:11,145
JD, just wait in the car.

894
00:53:11,279 --> 00:53:12,580
- I need to talk to you.
- Sir?

895
00:53:12,647 --> 00:53:13,648
I said wait.

896
00:53:17,185 --> 00:53:18,319
I understand.

897
00:53:18,353 --> 00:53:20,188
If they need to know your worth,

898
00:53:20,855 --> 00:53:22,190
a gap is essential.

899
00:53:24,225 --> 00:53:25,393
Your decision is correct.

900
00:53:26,060 --> 00:53:27,962
You wanted a break
for three months, right?

901
00:53:28,062 --> 00:53:29,063
I have okayed it.

902
00:53:30,932 --> 00:53:32,100
When did I ask?

903
00:53:37,639 --> 00:53:38,773
Isn't this your signature?

904
00:53:41,442 --> 00:53:42,277
Sir.

905
00:53:42,977 --> 00:53:44,379
Carbon copy, sir.

906
00:53:44,479 --> 00:53:45,813
Oh! Come on, JD.

907
00:53:46,681 --> 00:53:49,517
Haven't you opted for three months
break to teach?

908
00:53:49,651 --> 00:53:51,819
Teach? In which college?

909
00:53:52,854 --> 00:53:54,189
College?

910
00:53:54,355 --> 00:53:56,057
You have mentioned
Observation Home.

911
00:53:57,358 --> 00:53:59,227
Sir, don't play with me.

912
00:53:59,360 --> 00:54:00,695
What will I do there?

913
00:54:00,728 --> 00:54:01,896
I didn't sign this.

914
00:54:03,898 --> 00:54:06,100
Maybe after 6:00 p.m.?

915
00:54:10,605 --> 00:54:11,773
After 6:00 p.m.,

916
00:54:12,607 --> 00:54:13,808
there's a possibility.

917
00:54:13,942 --> 00:54:14,976
See.

918
00:54:15,643 --> 00:54:18,479
JD, you're losing control on yourself.

919
00:54:22,016 --> 00:54:25,520
If there's any issue in the election,
didn't you agree to resign your job?

920
00:54:26,187 --> 00:54:28,022
That means you had
something on your mind.

921
00:54:29,057 --> 00:54:30,558
Fine, sir, I'll go.

922
00:54:31,226 --> 00:54:33,194
Well, I've many well-wishers here.

923
00:54:33,228 --> 00:54:34,729
They must be behind this.

924
00:54:35,563 --> 00:54:37,599
It's okay, I need a change too, I'll go.

925
00:54:37,765 --> 00:54:41,102
Inspector is waiting in your lodge
to explain the job you'll be undertaking.

926
00:54:43,271 --> 00:54:44,772
That means.

927
00:54:45,440 --> 00:54:46,307
- Needhimani.
- Sir?

928
00:54:46,808 --> 00:54:48,309
You didn't pass on any information?

929
00:54:48,443 --> 00:54:49,644
No, sir.

930
00:54:51,646 --> 00:54:53,815
Then whatever lawyer
and I spoke in the union office,

931
00:54:53,848 --> 00:54:56,017
- How did the police get to hear?
- That's what puzzles me, sir.

932
00:54:59,020 --> 00:55:01,022
You know this music director Anirudh?

933
00:55:02,023 --> 00:55:03,391
He has composed a new film song.

934
00:55:04,058 --> 00:55:05,226
Shall we listen?

935
00:55:08,930 --> 00:55:10,398
- Listen.<i>-Sir...</i>

936
00:55:10,732 --> 00:55:13,601
<i>Bhavani has fixed the date.
You are his next target.</i>

937
00:55:13,768 --> 00:55:15,937
<i>He has decided to kill you too.</i>

938
00:55:16,271 --> 00:55:17,639
What do you say now, bigamist?

939
00:55:18,439 --> 00:55:20,875
At least is this your voice
or will you claim it's mimicry?

940
00:55:20,975 --> 00:55:22,610
- Sir.
- Did you call me, Bhavani?

941
00:55:25,146 --> 00:55:28,483
Make sure the boys are supplied
their regular dose of drinks and drugs.

942
00:55:29,017 --> 00:55:31,519
Whether they get
three square meals a day or not,

943
00:55:32,487 --> 00:55:34,589
booze and dope should flow steadily.

944
00:55:34,689 --> 00:55:36,224
Okay, Bhavani. I'll see to it.

945
00:55:38,359 --> 00:55:39,294
- Where was I?
- Sir.

946
00:55:39,394 --> 00:55:41,229
You got me married. How
can you make my wife a widow?

947
00:55:42,897 --> 00:55:43,898
- Tell me, sir.
- Wait.

948
00:55:44,098 --> 00:55:46,601
I'm choking with emotion
hearing your sentimental speech.

949
00:55:51,272 --> 00:55:52,607
Stop moving like that, will you?

950
00:55:52,974 --> 00:55:56,144
I had tucked the knife in my waist.
What if it pierces me in the wrong place?

951
00:55:56,978 --> 00:55:59,647
- Sir.
- Suppose an enemy kills us,

952
00:55:59,981 --> 00:56:02,350
doesn't matter if they say
that's how Bhavani died a noble death.

953
00:56:02,684 --> 00:56:06,154
If they say he had tucked a knife
that stabbed him in a wrong spot,

954
00:56:06,187 --> 00:56:07,455
does that sound good?

955
00:56:07,522 --> 00:56:08,957
- No.
- No, right?

956
00:56:09,057 --> 00:56:10,058
Won't sound good.

957
00:56:10,225 --> 00:56:12,126
- Lean back comfortably.
- Don't, sir.

958
00:56:12,227 --> 00:56:13,795
- Do you really respect me?
- Yes, sir.

959
00:56:13,895 --> 00:56:16,731
How come over the phone
all this kinship was missing?

960
00:56:16,898 --> 00:56:18,099
What is this?

961
00:56:18,600 --> 00:56:20,268
- Lean back.
- No, sir.

962
00:56:20,435 --> 00:56:22,503
Won't you listen to what I'm saying?

963
00:56:22,604 --> 00:56:24,606
Lean back. Sit, sit, sit!

964
00:56:24,639 --> 00:56:26,140
Lean back!

965
00:56:35,516 --> 00:56:36,684
Gopal!

966
00:56:38,186 --> 00:56:39,487
- Hey.
- Yes, sir.

967
00:56:40,688 --> 00:56:41,623
Tell me, sir.

968
00:56:41,689 --> 00:56:44,359
Ask Das to pick two boys
10, 15 years old to surrender.

969
00:56:44,392 --> 00:56:45,560
- Okay, sir.
- Go.

970
00:56:45,727 --> 00:56:46,728
Sir?

971
00:56:46,861 --> 00:56:49,731
A new master has been recruited
for our reformatory.

972
00:56:49,898 --> 00:56:51,599
- Okay. So?
- I didn't know if you knew.

973
00:56:51,766 --> 00:56:52,934
So I thought I should inform you.

974
00:56:53,067 --> 00:56:54,769
A teacher is bound to be appointed.

975
00:56:55,436 --> 00:56:58,106
All of you are giving a build up
as if it is breaking news!

976
00:56:58,606 --> 00:57:01,109
Dispose this body and
ask someone to drive this truck.

977
00:57:01,142 --> 00:57:01,976
Okay, sir.

978
00:57:04,145 --> 00:57:06,481
<i>Creep like a lioness, make no sound</i>

979
00:57:06,648 --> 00:57:09,517
<i>Slide like a snake over sun baked ground</i>

980
00:57:11,019 --> 00:57:12,854
Sir, can we switch off that cacophony.

981
00:57:12,987 --> 00:57:14,355
Then shall I wear my coolers?

982
00:57:15,557 --> 00:57:18,459
<i>Twist like a hurricane, bend and sway</i>

983
00:57:18,560 --> 00:57:21,729
<i>Break like a wave, wash the filth away</i>

984
00:57:28,436 --> 00:57:33,208
Sir, college students are bound by
certain protocols of parents and society,

985
00:57:33,308 --> 00:57:35,276
but those boys
lack all that discipline.

986
00:57:35,310 --> 00:57:38,646
Their age and their activities
have no connection whatsoever.

987
00:57:42,817 --> 00:57:44,819
<i>Not even a single inmate
is human or humane.</i>

988
00:57:45,853 --> 00:57:47,188
<i>Beasts.</i>

989
00:57:47,555 --> 00:57:49,224
- Kabaddi.<i>-Demons.</i>

990
00:57:49,357 --> 00:57:50,692
Kabaddi.

991
00:57:50,725 --> 00:57:53,895
<i>They know our law is lenient
to their habitual crimes.</i>

992
00:57:54,562 --> 00:57:57,265
<i>They use it to their advantage
breaking laws like reckless criminals.</i>

993
00:57:58,566 --> 00:57:59,934
<i>That's why, I'm telling you, sir.</i>

994
00:58:00,068 --> 00:58:01,336
Don't bend backwards to reform them

995
00:58:01,436 --> 00:58:03,404
in these three months
you are assigned there.

996
00:58:05,273 --> 00:58:08,109
Aren't you wondering
whether to go there or not?

997
00:58:08,810 --> 00:58:09,978
Sir?

998
00:58:10,645 --> 00:58:11,613
Sir!

999
00:58:12,847 --> 00:58:14,182
